<title>GERMANY: West German Apr industry output falls 1.4 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>West German Apr industry output falls 1.4 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Economics Ministry reported the following indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT    Apr 97     Mar 97     Apr 96</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   -1.4	 +0.1	 unch</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.1	 +2.5	 -1.6</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		95.7	 97.1	 94.7</p>
<p>The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				     Apr 97		  Mar 97</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining		     89.9	 +7.0     84.0	 -1.8</p>
<p> Manufacturing output   94.9	 -2.1     96.9	 unch</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   99.4	 -1.3    100.7	 -0.7</p>
<p>	Capital goods     95.8	 +1.3     94.6	 -2.8</p>
<p>	Consumer durables 83.6	 -9.8     92.7	+10.9</p>
<p>	Consumer goods    88.3	 -5.7     93.6	 +1.6</p>
<p> Energy output	   108.6	 +2.5    106.0	 +2.2</p>
<p> Construction	     96.3	 +0.4     95.9	 -0.2</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr-Mar 97 with Feb-Jan 97:</p>
<p>    Industrial production	    unch</p>
<p>Two month comparison Apr-Mar 97 with Apr-Mar 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +1.7</p>
<p> Mining				    -0.2</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +2.1</p>
<p>  Including:Intermediate goods     +3.7</p>
<p>		Capital goods	    +1.4</p>
<p>		Consumer durables	+6.2</p>
<p>		Consumer goods	   -3.2</p>
<p> Energy output			   -2.2</p>
<p> Construction			    +0.6</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 260 97 150</p>
</text>
